## 4. Methodology

### 4.1. Approach
The system is divided into two primary layers: the **Offline Compilation Pipeline (Python)** and the **Interactive Presentation Layer (HTML5/CSS3/JavaScript)**.

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Raw Unit Text Files] -->|Deterministic Parser compiler.py| B(Structured JSON Outputs)
    B -->|hierarchy.json| C[2D D3.js Force Graph]
    B -->|graph.json / vector_coords.json| D[3D Three.js Space Explorer]
    B -->|chunk_map.json| E[Textbook & Short Notes Viewer]
    
    C & D & E -->|Right-Click Selection| F[Local Ollama Inference Engine]
    F -->|MCQs / CIE / SEE Questions| G[Interactive Quiz Modal]
```

#### Explanation of the Processing Flow:
1. **Compilation Phase**: The developer inputs raw text study guides into the Python compiler. The compiler detects headings and structures via regex, building a hierarchy tree while ensuring 100% of the text survives.
2. **Rendering Phase**: The web client reads the generated JSON structures. D3.js builds the interactive nodes, and Three.js maps the concepts in a 3D starfield.
3. **Inference Phase**: When a user highlights text within the Textbook Viewer, a custom context menu catches the selection. The web client formats a prompt and sends an HTTP POST request to the local Ollama server, which returns structured quiz objects or explanatory sheets.

